sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: VM startup and shutdown
  accDescr: The VPN gateway starts before the VM boots. Guest tools and the proxy are then provisioned, and host tunnels become ready.
  participant U as User
  participant A as agents CLI
  participant H as Mac gateway / services
  participant V as Lima VM
  U->>A: agents create
  A->>V: Create stopped VM, save config
  U->>A: agents vpn add (optional, before first boot)
  A->>A: Validate profile, save VPN intent, replace NIC
  U->>A: agents start
  alt VPN configured
    A->>H: Install fallback guard, start sing-box and gateway
    H->>H: Detect trusted LAN, choose direct or VLESS
    H-->>A: Gateway ready
    A->>A: Verify the single guarded NIC and DNS
    A->>V: Boot with guarded networking
  else VPN disabled
    A->>V: Boot with ordinary Lima networking
  end
  V->>V: Provision tools on first boot
  A->>V: Install guest proxy and credentials
  A->>H: Start host policy / SOCKS daemon and SSH tunnels
  A->>V: Check proxy and tunnel readiness
  A-->>U: Ready for SSH, agents, or browser SOCKS
  U->>A: agents stop
  A->>H: Stop host proxy daemon and its tunnels
  A->>V: Stop VM and all guest sessions
  A->>H: Stop VPN gateway and client
